rranties in the United States. The company offers customizable home warranties that help customers to protect and maintain their homes from costly and unplanned breakdowns of essential home systems and appliances. Its home warranty customers subscribe to an annual service plan agreement that covers the repair or replacement of principal components of home systems and appliances, including electrical, plumbing, water heaters, refrigerators, dishwashers, and ranges/ovens/cooktops, as well as pools, spas, and pumps; and heating, ventilation, and air conditioning systems. It also offers non-warranty home services through website and application; a one-stop app experience for home repair and maintenance using video chat, augmented reality, and computer vision and machining learning. The company operates under the American Home Shield, HSA, OneGuard, Landmark, and 2-10 HBW brand names. Frontdoor, Inc. was founded in 1971 and is headquartered in Memphis, Tennessee.","ceo_bio":"Mr. William C. Cobb | Chairman of the Board & CEO | Age 68 | Compensation: $2.8M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $1.0M ranks in the top quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers, with revenue growing 8%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $192K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $17K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["frontdoor, inc. is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $6.5B market cap on $2.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +8% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 39% against a 9% cost of capital \u2014 a 30-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat, with gross margins sitting at 49%.","The business throws off $390M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 19 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.63\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 5.3\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 4.3% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 2.5\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.20866408221032676},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.9% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $23.9M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Significant goodwill (45% of assets) from past acquisitions \u2014 a soft asset a conservative appraisal discounts to zero","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 12% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Piotroski score 9/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Financial quality scores above most Consumer Cyclical peers","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"What Frontdoor (FTDR)'s Earnings Beat Means For Shareholders","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/consumer-services/nasdaq-ftdr/frontdoor/news/what-frontdoor-ftdrs-earnings-beat-means-for-shareholders","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794612679.608,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.296,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"We Think Frontdoor's (NASDAQ:FTDR) Solid Earnings Are Understated","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/consumer-services/nasdaq-ftdr/frontdoor/news/we-think-frontdoors-nasdaqftdr-solid-earnings-are-understate","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794483449.195,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.542,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"(FTDR) Price Dynamics and Execution-Aware Positioning","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/21/FTDR_Price_Dynamics_and_Execution-Aware_Positioning_111126100802_1794409682.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794409682.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.494,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Critical Analysis: Frontdoor (NASDAQ:FTDR) & Carriage Services (NYSE:CSV)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/10/critical-analysis-frontdoor-nasdaqftdr-carriage-services-nysecsv.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794330991.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.876,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Fro